-- title:
--   Congruent form with integral q-expansion modulo 𝔪
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$, let $H'$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/N)^\times$, let $k \in \mathbb Z$, let $p$ be a prime, and let $\mathfrak m$ be a prime ideal of the ring $\overline{\mathbb Z} = \mathrm{integralClosure}\ \mathbb Z\ \mathbb C$ of algebraic integers in $\mathbb C$ with $p \in \mathfrak m$. Let $Y$ be a modular form of weight $k$ for [`CohCarrier.GammaH N H'`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the image in $SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ of the subgroup of $\Gamma_0(N)$ consisting of those matrices whose associated unit $d \bmod N$ (the homomorphism `gamma0Units`) lies in $H'$. Write $a_n(Y) =$ `qCoeff Y n` for the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $Y$ of width $1$. Assume: (i) every $a_n(Y)$ is $\mathfrak m$-integral, in the sense that there are algebraic integers $x, y$ with $y \notin \mathfrak m$ and $x = y\,a_n(Y)$ in $\mathbb C$; (ii) each $a_n(Y)$ reduces modulo $\mathfrak m$ into the image of $\mathbb Z$, in the sense that for each $n$ there is $m \in \mathbb Z$ with $x - m y \in \mathfrak m$ for all algebraic integers $x, y$ such that $y \notin \mathfrak m$ and $x = y\,a_n(Y)$. Then there exist a modular form $Y'$ of weight $k$ for the same group and a power series $P \in \mathbb Z[\![q]\!]$ such that the image of $P$ under $\mathbb Z \to \mathbb C$ is the $q$-expansion of $Y'$ of width $1$, and such that for every $n$ and all algebraic integers $x, y$ with $y \notin \mathfrak m$ and $x = y\,a_n(Y)$ one has $x - (\text{coeff}_n P)\, y \in \mathfrak m$; that is, $a_n(Y) \equiv \text{coeff}_n P \pmod{\mathfrak m}$ for all $n$.
--
--   This is the passage from a form whose Fourier coefficients are $\mathfrak m$-integral with reductions in the prime field to an honest form of the same weight and level having a rational-integral $q$-expansion congruent to it modulo $\mathfrak m$. It is used in the comparison of the fields generated by $q$-expansions of integral forms on $\Gamma_H(N)$, in [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_le_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_infSubgroup`](thm.html#ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_le_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_infSubgroup).
